/**
 * Pendle PRICE-FLOOR fixtures — RAW `POST /v3/sdk/1/convert` response bodies,
 * captured verbatim from the LIVE hosted API. Nothing here is synthesized.
 *
 * PROVENANCE
 *   URL      : https://api-v2.pendle.finance/core/v3/sdk/1/convert  (chain 1)
 *   Date     : 2026-07-27
 *   Cost     : quote-only. Convert BUILDS calldata; it signs nothing, broadcasts
 *              nothing, and needs no key. 7 CU per call, HTTP 201 on all 11.
 *   Market   : wstETH, `0x34280882267ffa6383b363e278b027be083bbe3b` (the deepest
 *              chain-1 book at capture time, ~$3.56M) — except `rollOverPt`,
 *              whose destination leg is the 27AUG2026 wstETH market
 *              `0xba1cbaece600beec76dabc0a4ead31e0339cbe37`.
 *   Amount   : 1e18 of the input leg on every capture (1e9 USDC for
 *              `buyPtAggregator`, whose point is the aggregator, not the size).
 *   Slippage : 100 bps on every capture (see {@link PENDLE_FLOOR_FIXTURE_SLIPPAGE_BPS}).
 *
 * SCRUB APPLIED
 *   `receiver` / `tx.from` is `0x742d35Cc6634C0532925a3b844Bc454e4438f44e` — a
 *   public exchange address this repo already uses as its pseudonymous Pendle
 *   fixture receiver (`fixtures.ts`). No wallet of ours appears here and no
 *   position was read: a convert quote is built for whatever receiver it is
 *   handed, so the address is a placeholder, not a holder. Every other value —
 *   market/PT/YT/LP/SY addresses, amounts, calldata — is public protocol data
 *   reproduced verbatim. NOTHING was removed or edited; a scrubbed field would
 *   break the decode these fixtures exist to exercise.
 *
 * ROUTE LISTS TRUNCATED, VALUES NOT: each capture keeps its first two routes
 * (`buyPtAggregator` keeps one KyberSwap and one OKX route so the pendleSwap
 * pin is exercised against both extRouter shapes). Every RETAINED route is
 * byte-for-byte what the API returned; only the LENGTH of `routes[]` differs
 * from the wire — no value inside a retained route was touched.
 *
 * NON-EMPTY BY CONSTRUCTION (rule 90, "Verification Discipline"): every capture
 * carries at least one route with real calldata and a real min-out. A fixture
 * that only encoded the empty collection is what let a prediction read pass for
 * months without ever validating a row.
 *
 * WHAT THEY PROVE (measured, not assumed — see the R5a report):
 *   - Pendle embeds `floor(output × (10000 − slippageBps) / 10000)` EXACTLY.
 *     Our independently computed floor matched the provider's own min-out to the
 *     ATOMIC UNIT (delta 0) on 10 of 11 captures, including the aggregator route.
 *   - `addLiquiditySingleToken` is the one exception and it errs SAFE: the
 *     provider's minLpOut sat 2791205212855374 raw units ABOVE our floor
 *     (~0.5% haircut against the 1% requested), so the guard passes it.
 *   - `mintPyFromToken` carries ONE `minPyOut`, not a minPtOut/minYtOut pair;
 *     the response's two outputs (PT and YT) are EQUAL by protocol.
 *   - `callAndReflect`'s leg-1 receiver is the REFLECTOR
 *     (`0x30544e00cf296b34a9ee59e5540ae2f9cccd55dd`), leg-2's is the wallet.
 */

